  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given two positive integers `A` and `B`, your task is to calculate and print their greatest common divisor (GCD).\n\nThe **Greatest Common Divisor (GCD)** of two numbers is the largest positive integer that divides both numbers without leaving a remainder using recursion.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nA single line containing two space separated integers `A` and `B`.\n\n\nOutput Format\n\nPrint a single integer: the GCD of `A` and `B`",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= T <= 1000",
      "1 <= A <= 1000",
      "1 <= B <= 1000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "First line contains an integer T, the number of test cases. Each test case contains two space-separated positive integers A and B.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing the greatest common divisor of A and B.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n3 18\n1 10\n12 15",
        "output": "3\n1\n3",
        "explanation": "Test case 1: gcd(3,18)=3. Test case 2: gcd(1,10)=1. Test case 3: gcd(12,15)=3."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n7 13",
        "output": "1",
        "explanation": "Only 1 divides both 7 and 13, so the GCD is 1."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "2\n100 10\n81 27",
        "output": "10\n27",
        "explanation": "gcd(100,10)=10; gcd(81,27)=27."
      }
    ]
  },
